@page "/Upload"
@model Pegasus.Web.Pages.UploadModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Upload";
}

@* A surface of its own, not a panel wedged above the Inbox list. The words
   "Receive intake", "Queue instruction" and "Original bytes are retained
   before durable processing" are all gone: the first two are pipeline
   vocabulary, and the third narrates storage at someone who just wants to
   send a file. *@
<header class="page-heading">
    <h1>Upload</h1>
</header>

@* One thing happens here, so the form is a bounded column rather than a panel
   floating at full page width; what happens after the button sits beside it,
   because the status page is the wrong place to learn that for the first
   time. *@
<div class="upload-layout">
    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="upload-title">
        <h2 id="upload-title" class="section-label">Upload documents or images</h2>
        <form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">
            <input asp-for="ExternalReceiptToken" type="hidden" />
            <div asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly" class="validation-summary-errors" role="alert"></div>
            @* The dashed area is the destination. site.js makes the whole
               of it a drop target and gives it a real button; the native
               input stays the control underneath and is the visible
               control when script is off. *@
            <div class="dropzone" data-dropzone>
                <span class="dropzone__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon icon--lg"><use href="#icon-upload" /></svg></span>
                <label asp-for="Upload">Drag files here, or choose them</label>
                @* The accepted types are stated, not left in an `accept`
                   attribute the operator cannot read. *@
                <span class="field-hint">E-mail, Word document, PDF or image — up to @Pegasus.Web.Pages.UploadModel.MaximumSizeLabel.</span>
                <input asp-for="Upload" type="file" multiple accept=".eml,.pdf,.docx,.doc,.msg,.jpg,.jpeg,.png,message/rfc822,application/pdf,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document,application/msword,application/vnd.ms-outlook,image/jpeg,image/png" />
                <button type="button" class="btn dropzone__browse" hidden data-dropzone-browse>Choose files</button>
                <p class="dropzone__file" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden data-dropzone-file></p>
            </div>
            <span asp-validation-for="Upload" class="field-validation-error"></span>
            <button type="submit" class="primary-action primary-action--block">Upload</button>
        </form>
    </section>

    @* Every sentence here is the real flow: the receipt is durable before the
       page redirects (Upload.cshtml.cs), the status page refreshes itself
       while the state is Received or Processing (UploadStatus), and Complete
       links to the case or the retained receipt. Nothing is promised that the
       Worker does not do. *@
    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="upload-next-title">
        <h2 id="upload-next-title" class="section-label">What happens next</h2>
        <ol class="upload-steps">
            <li><b>The file is kept as received.</b><span>You get a receipt the moment it is stored.</span></li>
            <li><b>It is processed in the background.</b><span>The status page refreshes itself until processing is complete.</span></li>
            <li><b>Open the result.</b><span>A case created from the file, or the retained receipt when no case was created; a failure is stated on the status page.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <h2 class="section-label section-gap">Accepted files</h2>
        <ul class="accepted-list" aria-label="Accepted file types">
            <li>.eml</li><li>.msg</li><li>.pdf</li><li>.doc</li><li>.docx</li><li>.jpg</li><li>.png</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="field-hint">Up to @Pegasus.Web.Pages.UploadModel.MaximumSizeLabel each. Select as many as needed.</p>
    </section>
</div>
